# CompTIA A+ — Networking

Wi-Fi 5 is the marketing name for 802.11{{ac}}.
---
Wi-Fi 4 is 802.11n, Wi-Fi 6 is 802.11ax.

Wi-Fi 6 is the marketing name for 802.11{{ax}}.
---
Adds OFDMA and works on both 2.4 and 5 GHz. Wi-Fi 6E extends it to 6 GHz.

Which two frequency bands does 802.11n use?
---
2.4 GHz and 5 GHz
= 2.4 and 5 GHz
= 2.4/5 GHz
= 5 GHz and 2.4 GHz
= 5 and 2.4 GHz
= 2.4 and 5
= 5 and 2.4
---
2.4 GHz travels farther but is crowded. 5 GHz is faster with more channels.

An address in 169.254.0.0/16 means the client failed to reach a {{DHCP}} server.
---
APIPA, Automatic Private IP Addressing. The machine self-assigns and can only talk to the local link.

What is the private class C address range?
---
192.168.0.0 to 192.168.255.255
= 192.168.0.0/16
= 192.168.x.x
= 192.168.0.0 - 192.168.255.255
---
The other private ranges: 10.0.0.0/8 and 172.16.0.0 to 172.31.255.255.

The private class A range is {{10}}.0.0.0/8.
---
Sixteen million addresses. Common in large corporate networks.

What is the default subnet mask for a /24 network?
---
255.255.255.0
---
254 usable host addresses.

Which DNS record type maps a hostname to an IPv4 address?
---
A
= A record
---
AAAA maps to IPv6. MX names the mail server. CNAME is an alias.

Which DNS record type directs a domain's incoming mail?
---
MX
= MX record
= mail exchange
= mail exchanger

Which device connects a LAN to the internet and picks paths between networks?
---
router
= a router
---
A switch forwards frames inside one LAN by MAC address. The router works at layer 3.

What does NAT do?
---
Translates private IP addresses to a public one
~ Assigns IP addresses to clients automatically
~ Resolves hostnames to IP addresses
~ Encrypts traffic between networks
---
It is how a whole home LAN shares one public IPv4 address.

Which service assigns IP addresses to clients automatically?
---
DHCP
= dynamic host configuration protocol
---
It leases the address, mask, gateway, and DNS servers.

Which network type is a smartphone's Bluetooth connection an example of?
---
PAN
= personal area network
---
LAN is a building, WAN spans cities, MAN spans a metro area.

What does a switch use to decide which port a frame goes out?
---
MAC address
= MAC
= MAC addresses
= the MAC address
---
It learns which MAC lives on which port and forwards instead of broadcasting.

Which command shows your IP address on Windows?
---
ipconfig
---
ipconfig /all adds MAC, DHCP, and DNS detail. Linux and macOS use ip addr or ifconfig.

Which command traces the route packets take to a host on Windows?
---
tracert
---
Linux and macOS call it traceroute. Each hop is a router along the path.
